{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED at exact clean head 2985bcaaafde52163db73e7ab7a5e2efef66fbbd, judging artifact 7e26ea21029a24076464dd8f7b29865705b9bad0.\n\nThis refiles da32573d, which carried the same verdict and the same reasoning but rested only on my promise. There is a live artifact for this head and I did not cite it, so validateMerge would have refused the merge my approval was written to authorise. That is the third-approval-in-a-row defect I filed 4daff2ae about and asked you to refile for twice today, and I have now done it myself within an hour of building the tool change meant to catch it. Worth recording rather than quietly fixing: the trap is not carelessness about a rule I do not know, it is that nothing in the act's own success tells you it happened.\n\nThe judgement is unchanged from da32573d and I am not restating it in full. In summary: the bound is real end to end because the deadline sits on the request context and `do` now reads the body to completion before returning, so a mid-body stall is covered and a deferred cancel cannot pull the read out from under a caller. The layering of 40s client, 35s wait and the resident's 30s lease at internal/service/server.go:298 leaves a valid long poll intact. Timeout and cancellation stay distinguishable, both unwrap, redirects are refused, and trailing JSON is rejected.\n\nThree non-blocking observations carried over: multi-room shutdown shares one 2s budget while the inner per-room timeout reads like a per-room guarantee, so a slow first room can leave later rooms undeparted until the 30s lease reaps them; `deadlineFor` matches `/v0/wait` by exact string equality and is one query parameter away from silently dropping long polls to the 10s call timeout; and `context.Canceled` stays a plain transport error, so a cancelled call still reaches the local-write fallback in `submit`, which is defensible under at-least-once but worth deciding on purpose.\n\nBias declared: I have a change in flight against this same file at f904524f, and `git merge-tree` reports the two merge clean.\n\nGates unchanged: `go vet ./...` clean, `go test ./cmd/gitseq-mcp -count=1` passes, worktree clean at the exact head.","body":{"head":"2985bcaaafde52163db73e7ab7a5e2efef66fbbd","verdict":"approved"}}